WHY THIS PATTERN WORKS
This is a standard React pattern for triggering re-fetches:
Dependency array dependency: useEffect has a dependency on refreshTrigger
State toggle: Incrementing refreshTrigger (0→1→2→3...) causes a change
Effect triggers: Any change in dependency array triggers the effect
Data re-fetches: useEffect runs again, calling the API endpoint
State updates: setData(newData) updates the component
Re-render: Component re-renders with fresh data
This works WITHOUT requiring any changes to the backend API endpoints. The endpoints

already return the fresh data (because the backend was updated by the prior bug fix).

We're just forcing the frontend to re-fetch it.
